table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>model_key</th>\n      <th>model_name</th>\n      <th>status</th>\n      <th>context_length</th>\n      <th>model_revision</th>\n      <th>error</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>gpt2</td>\n      <td>gpt2</td>\n      <td>SUCCESS</td>\n      <td>1024</td>\n      <td>607a30d783dfa663caf39e06633721c8d4cfcd7e</td>\n      <td></td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>pythia_410m</td>\n      <td>EleutherAI/pythia-410m</td>\n      <td>SUCCESS</td>\n      <td>2048</td>\n      <td>9879c9b5f8bea9051dcb0e68dff21493d67e9d4f</td>\n      <td></td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>2</th>\n      <td>qwen2_5_0_5b</td>\n      <td>Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B</td>\n      <td>SUCCESS</td>\n      <td>32768</td>\n      <td>060db6499f32faf8b98477b0a26969ef7d8b9987</td>\n      <td></td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>3</th>\n      <td>tinyllama_1_1b</td>\n      <td>TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0</td>\n      <td>SUCCESS</td>\n      <td>2048</td>\n      <td>fe8a4ea1ffedaf415f4da2f062534de366a451e6</td>\n      <td></td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":6},{"id":"9942e2e4","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 5. Score chunks and build binned frequency distributions\n\nEach paper's chunks are scored identically across models. The score is BPC (total negative log-likelihood in bits divided by the original chunk's character count). For every paper/model pair, an adaptive histogram is formed with at most 30 bins; the stored distribution contains bin boundaries, centers, and integer frequencies, not a normalized probability column. Source moments are calculated as frequency-weighted moments of the bin centers.","metadata":{"editable":false}},{"id":"c8614e61","cell_type":"code","source":"def score_chunk_bpc(text, tokenizer, model, context_length, stride=STRIDE):\n    text_for_model = text.lower() if LOWERCASE_FOR_LM else text\n    character_count = len(text_for_model)\n    encoded = tokenizer(\n        text_for_model,\n        return_tensors=\"pt\",\n        add_special_tokens=False,\n    )\n    input_ids = encoded[\"input_ids\"].to(DEVICE)\n    sequence_length = int(input_ids.shape[1])\n\n    if sequence_length < 2 or character_count == 0:\n        return {\n            \"bpc\": np.nan,\n            \"bits_per_token\": np.nan,\n            \"perplexity\": np.nan,\n            \"total_bits\": np.nan,\n            \"scored_tokens\": 0,\n            \"model_tokens\": sequence_length,\n            \"character_count\": character_count,\n        }\n\n    effective_stride = max(1, min(int(stride), context_length - 1))\n    total_nll_nats = 0.0\n    scored_tokens = 0\n    target_start = 1\n\n    with torch.inference_mode():\n        while target_start < sequence_length:\n            target_end = min(target_start + effective_stride, sequence_length)\n            window_start = max(0, target_end - context_length)\n            window = input_ids[:, window_start:target_end]\n\n            outputs = model(input_ids=window)\n            shifted_logits = outputs.logits[:, :-1, :]\n            shifted_labels = window[:, 1:]\n\n            local_start = target_start - window_start - 1\n            local_end = target_end - window_start - 1\n\n            if local_start < 0 or local_end > shifted_labels.shape[1]:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"Sliding-window target indices are out of range.\")\n\n            selected_logits = shifted_logits[:, local_start:local_end, :].float()\n            selected_labels = shifted_labels[:, local_start:local_end]\n\n            if selected_labels.numel() == 0:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"No target tokens were selected for scoring.\")\n\n            nll_sum = torch.nn.functional.cross_entropy(\n                selected_logits.reshape(-1, selected_logits.shape[-1]),\n                selected_labels.reshape(-1),\n                reduction=\"sum\",\n            )\n            total_nll_nats += float(nll_sum.item())\n            scored_tokens += int(selected_labels.numel())\n            target_start = target_end\n\n    if scored_tokens != sequence_length - 1:\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            f\"Token accounting mismatch: scored {scored_tokens} of {sequence_length - 1} targets.\"\n        )\n\n    total_bits = total_nll_nats / math.log(2.0)\n    mean_nll_nats = total_nll_nats / scored_tokens\n    return {\n        \"bpc\": total_bits / character_count,\n        \"bits_per_token\": total_bits / scored_tokens,\n        \"perplexity\": math.exp(mean_nll_nats) if mean_nll_nats < 50 else np.inf,\n        \"total_bits\": total_bits,\n        \"scored_tokens\": scored_tokens,\n        \"model_tokens\": sequence_length,\n        \"character_count\": character_count,\n    }\n\ndef make_frequency_histogram(values, min_bins=MIN_BINS, max_bins=MAX_BINS):\n    values = np.asarray(values, dtype=float)\n    values = values[np.isfinite(values)]\n    if values.size == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Cannot bin an empty set of BPC values.\")\n\n    if values.size == 1 or np.isclose(float(values.min()), float(values.max())):\n        center = float(values[0])\n        edges = np.array([center - 0.5, center + 0.5], dtype=float)\n    else:\n        fd_edges = np.histogram_bin_edges(values, bins=\"fd\")\n        proposed_bins = max(1, len(fd_edges) - 1)\n        bin_count = int(np.clip(proposed_bins, min_bins, max_bins))\n        edges = np.linspace(float(values.min()), float(values.max()), bin_count + 1)\n\n    counts, edges = np.histogram(values, bins=edges)\n    centers = (edges[:-1] + edges[1:]) / 2\n    nonempty = counts > 0\n    return pd.DataFrame({\n        \"bin_left\": edges[:-1][nonempty],\n        \"bin_right\": edges[1:][nonempty],\n        \"bin_center\": centers[nonempty],\n        \"frequency\": counts[nonempty].astype(int),\n    })\n\ndef moments_from_frequencies(histogram):\n    cen